Trigger: Your Pokémon misses with a Poison-Type Move
Effect: Your Pokémon may use either Smokescreen or Poison Gas as if they were on their Move List. When used this way, these Moves ignore Frequency Limitations, and are used as a Ranged Blast 3, with the blast centered on the square targeted by the triggering attack. Poison-Type Pokémon are not negatively affected by Smoke Screens created this way. Your Pokémon may also trigger Miasma deliberately as a Standard Action. In Acid Rain Weather Conditions, Miasma may be used ignoring Frequency, and your Pokémon may trigger Miasma deliberately as a Rapid Action.
